Amerika OS GRUB theme
=====================

This directory (/usr/share/grub/themes/amerika) holds a GRUB 2 theme. Installing amerika-branding does NOT
enable it and never edits /etc/default/grub, /boot or the EFI System Partition.

To try it (you are responsible for a working boot loader; keep the previous setting so you can revert):

  1. Copy the line GRUB_THEME (if any) from /etc/default/grub somewhere safe.
  2. As root, append to /etc/default/grub:
         GRUB_THEME=/usr/share/grub/themes/amerika/theme.txt
         GRUB_GFXMODE=1920x1080,auto
         GRUB_TERMINAL_OUTPUT=gfxterm
  3. Run: update-grub
  4. To revert, remove those lines again and run update-grub.

The theme was generated by flavor/tools/make_grub_theme.py. Its rendering is not verified on real hardware.
